  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian response for people affected by cyclone Ditwah in Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Ditwah made landfall in Sri Lanka on 28 November 2025, causing widespread flooding and landslides across the country, resulting in significant loss of life and extensive damage to homes, infrastructure, and essential services. Through this project, IOM is delivering urgent, life-saving Shelter and Non-Food Item (NFI) assistance to cyclone-affected households to mitigate immediate risks, prevent further loss of life, and restore minimum standards of safety and dignity.</narrative>
  </description>
